957	    }
958	
959	    /// Drain the accumulated events, appending a synthesized
960	    /// [`SessionEvent::ToolReturned`] for every [`SessionEvent::ToolCalled`]
961	    /// left without a matching result (a run cancelled/timed out mid-tool).
962	    /// The returned log always [`project`]s to a provider-valid conversation.
963	    ///
964	    /// On a resume, the log starts with the results of the resumed calls (and
965	    /// a synthesized result for each resumed call without one), then the
966	    /// recorded input and run events. A rejected resume returns no events.
967	    ///
968	    /// The match is by position, because a call id can repeat in one run: a
969	    /// `ToolCalled` event is closed only by a later `ToolReturned` (or
970	    /// `ToolDeferred`) event with the same call id, and each later event
